+# Reusable Component Library — NTCAS Accounting
+
+A reference inventory of UI primitives and patterns worth building **once** as
+shared components, instead of re-solving per feature. Grouped by purpose, with
+why it matters *for this specific app* (chart of accounts, vouchers, master
+data, reports) and what it would replace.
+
+> **How to use this file:** before building new UI, check `src/components/shared/`
+> (and this doc) for an existing pattern that fits. Reuse over rebuild, unless
+> the fit is genuinely poor — this doc is meant to *inform judgment*, not to
+> force every dropdown into a Combobox or every table into the generic factory.
+> Update the relevant section here whenever a component listed below actually
+> gets built, so this stays a map of what exists, not just what's planned.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Input & Selection
+
+### Combobox (searchable select)
+Text input + filterable dropdown, single-select. Type to narrow, click to pick.
+**Replaces:** every plain `<select>` currently used for Account Group, Sub-Group,
+Area, Sub-Area, Agent pickers. Fine today at 10–50 rows; becomes unusable once
+Ledger or Party lists grow past ~100 rows — this is your highest-leverage build,
+because nearly every voucher and master form needs "pick a ledger."
+
+### Async Combobox
+Same as above, but options are fetched from the API as the user types
+(debounced), instead of loading the full list upfront.
+**Where:** Ledger picker on Journal/Cash-Bank Voucher lines, Party picker —
+once you have thousands of ledgers/parties, loading them all client-side on
+every form mount is wasteful.
+
+### Multi-select / Tag input
+Pick several values into a pill-list, with typeahead.
+**Where:** report filters ("show these 5 account groups"), bulk-tagging
+parties to multiple sub-areas if that need ever comes up.
+
+### Date Picker / Date Range Picker
+Calendar popover instead of relying on the raw `<input type="date">`.
+**Where:** `voucherDate` on Journal/Cash-Bank Vouchers, fiscal year date
+ranges, report date filters (Trial Balance, Ledger reports all need "as of"
+or "from–to" ranges).
+
+### Currency / Decimal Input
+Formats as the user types (thousand separators, fixed decimal places),
+strips formatting on submit, enforces the schema's `Decimal(18,6)` precision.
+**Where:** every debit/credit field on voucher lines, credit limits, amounts.
+Right now a plain number input risks floating-point drift and inconsistent
+decimal display — this is a correctness issue, not just polish.
+
+### Masked / Pattern Input
+Enforces a format while typing (PAN number, phone number).
+**Where:** `Party.panNo`, `Party.phone`/`mobile` — catches malformed data at
+entry instead of at the database constraint.
+
+### File / Attachment Upload
+Drag-drop or click-to-browse, with preview and progress.
+**Where:** not in the schema yet, but standard for vouchers in any real
+accounting system (attach a scanned bill/receipt to a Cash-Bank Voucher). Good
+one to design for even before the schema supports it.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Data Display
+
+### Data Table (server-driven)
+Sortable columns, server-side pagination/filtering, column visibility toggle.
+**Replaces:** the current pattern where every table (`GroupsTable`,
+`AreasTable`, etc.) fetches *all* rows and does search/sort/paginate
+client-side. That's fine for Account Groups (dozens of rows) but will not
+scale to Ledgers, Parties, or voucher listings (thousands of rows,
+fiscal-year-scoped). This is the second-highest-leverage build after
+Combobox.
+
+### Virtualized List
+Renders only the rows in the visible viewport, even with 10,000+ items.
+**Where:** Ledger/Party pickers and any full Chart-of-Accounts browse view,
+once data volume grows.
+
+### Tree View
+Expand/collapse hierarchical nodes with indentation and connecting lines.
+**Where:** the Chart of Accounts is *already* a tree (Account Type → Group →
+Sub-Group → Ledger, and `GeneralLedger` even self-references via
+`parentId`/`GLHierarchy`). Right now this hierarchy is shown as separate flat
+pages linked by breadcrumbs — a real tree view would let someone browse the
+whole chart in one place, which is a natural "Chart of Accounts" report page.
+
+### Badge / Status Pill
+You already have `StatusBadge`, `AccountTypeBadge`, `GLTypeBadge` —
+worth formalizing into one generic `<Badge tone="success|warning|danger|neutral">`
+so every future enum (`DocumentType`, `InstrumentType`, posting status) gets
+consistent styling for free instead of a new one-off component each time.
+
+### Empty State
+Consistent "no data yet" illustration + message + call-to-action button.
+**Where:** you already hand-write `"No areas match your filters."` per table;
+a shared component keeps the tone and layout consistent and makes the CTA
+("+ Create your first Ledger") a standard pattern instead of an afterthought.
+
+### Skeleton Loader
+Gray placeholder blocks shown while data loads, instead of a blank screen or
+spinner.
+**Where:** becomes relevant the moment any list moves from server-rendered
+(current pattern, no loading state needed) to client-fetched — e.g. reports
+that run a calculation and take a moment.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Feedback & Overlays
+
+### Toast / Notification system
+Non-blocking "Saved successfully" / "Failed to delete" messages that appear
+and auto-dismiss.
+**Replaces:** the current pattern of inline red error boxes inside each form
+(`AreaForm`, `AccountGroupForm`, etc.), which is fine for *validation* errors
+but has no equivalent for *success* confirmation — right now success is
+silent (just a redirect). A toast system is one component, used everywhere.
+
+### Modal / Dialog (generic)
+You already have `ConfirmDialog` — worth generalizing into a base `<Modal>`
+that `ConfirmDialog` and future dialogs (e.g. "Quick add Ledger" without
+leaving the voucher form) both build on, instead of every new dialog being a
+bespoke fixed-positioned div.
+
+### Drawer / Slide-over panel
+Side panel that slides in over the current page — good for "quick view" or
+"quick create" without a full page navigation.
+**Where:** e.g. clicking a Ledger code on a voucher line to peek at its
+balance/details without losing your place in the voucher you're building.
+
+### Tooltip
+Small hover/focus label for icon-only buttons or truncated text.
+**Where:** the icon-only action buttons already in every table (Eye/Pencil/
+Trash2) rely on `title=` attributes today — real tooltips are more
+discoverable and consistent, especially on touch devices where hover doesn't
+exist.
+
+### Popover
+Anchored floating panel for richer content than a tooltip (e.g. a mini form
+or a preview card).
+**Where:** "show ledger balance" on hover/click in a voucher line, without a
+full drawer.
+
+### Command Palette (⌘K / Ctrl+K)
+Global fuzzy-search overlay to jump to any master, ledger, or action from
+anywhere in the app.
+**Where:** genuinely high-value for an app with this many nav sections
+(Master, Transactions, Inventory, Reports, Analysis, FM Analysis, Setup...) —
+the sidebar alone has 100+ links. This is the single biggest "feels modern"
+upgrade you can ship.
+
+---
+
+## 4. Forms & Validation
+
+### Schema-driven form + validation (e.g. a Zod schema per model)
+Right now every form (`AreaForm`, `AccountGroupForm`, `SubGroupForm`...)
+hand-rolls `useState` per field and manual `if (!x) setError(...)` checks.
+A shared `useForm` pattern with schema validation would:
+- eliminate repeated boilerplate across ~15+ forms,
+- give field-level (not just form-level) error messages,
+- keep client validation and API validation in sync from one source of truth.
+This is worth doing **before** you build many more masters — every one you
+build without it is more code to migrate later.
+
+### Dynamic Line-Item Editor (repeatable field groups)
+Add/remove rows, each with its own set of fields, with live totals.
+**Where this matters most:** `JournalVoucherLine` and `CashBankVoucherLine`
+are exactly this shape — a voucher has N lines, each with a ledger, debit,
+credit, narration. This component (with a live running debit/credit total,
+enforcing they balance to zero before submit) is the core of the entire
+Transactions module you haven't built yet. Build it once, reuse for Journal
+Voucher, Cash/Bank Voucher, Sales, Purchase, Debit/Credit Notes.
+
+### Multi-step Wizard
+Breaks a long form into steps with a progress indicator.
+**Where:** voucher entry (header → lines → review) or a "New Company Setup"
+onboarding flow under Setup.
+
+### Inline-edit table cell
+Click a cell, it becomes an input, blur/enter saves.
+**Where:** quick status toggles or code corrections directly from a list
+table, without a full navigate-to-edit-page round trip.
+
+---
+
+## 5. Navigation & Layout
+
+### Breadcrumbs (componentized)
+You already write breadcrumbs inline on every page
+(`Area Master > Add New Area`) — worth extracting to a `<Breadcrumbs items={...}>`
+component so the separator, styling, and truncation behavior are defined once.
+
+### Tabs (componentized)
+Same story — the Groups/Sub-Groups and Areas/Sub-Areas tab bars are currently
+hand-written per table. A generic `<Tabs>` component removes duplication as
+you add more paired masters.
+
+### Sticky/persistent filter bar
+Keeps search/filter controls visible while scrolling a long table.
+**Where:** any report or master list that grows long (Ledgers, Parties,
+voucher listings).
+
+---
+
+## 6. Domain-Specific (Accounting)
+
+### Debit/Credit Balance Indicator
+A live-updating strip showing "Total Debit: X | Total Credit: Y | Difference: Z",
+turning green when balanced, red when not.
+**Where:** essential UX for Journal Voucher and Cash/Bank Voucher entry —
+double-entry bookkeeping requires this to be visible at all times while
+building a voucher, not just checked on submit.
+
+### Amount-in-Words display
+Converts a numeric amount to its written-out form (e.g. "One Thousand Two
+Hundred and Fifty only") — standard on printed vouchers/cheques in South
+Asian accounting software.
+**Where:** voucher print view, cheque printing (`instrumentType: CHEQUE` on
+`CashBankVoucherLine` already implies this is coming).
+
+### Fiscal Year Switcher
+Global control (likely in the header/sidebar) to switch the active fiscal
+year context, since `fiscalYear` is already a field on both voucher models.
+**Where:** affects almost every report and transaction list — worth making a
+single global piece of state/UI rather than a per-page dropdown.
+
+### Posting/Approval Status Stepper
+Visual step indicator (Draft → Posted → [Reversed]) reflecting
+`isPosted`/`postedAt`/`reversalOfId` already in the schema.
+**Where:** voucher detail view — makes the audit trail visually obvious
+instead of just a boolean badge.
+
+### Ledger Balance Preview
+Small inline card showing a ledger's current/running balance when it's
+selected in a picker or viewed in a list.
+**Where:** pairs naturally with the Ledger Combobox above — genuinely useful
+the moment transactions start posting.
+
+---
+
+## 7. Bulk Operations & Automation
+
+### Bulk Import (CSV/Excel mapping wizard)
+Upload a spreadsheet, map columns to fields, preview, then batch-create.
+**Where:** high-value for master data — onboarding a company's entire
+existing Chart of Accounts, Party list, or Ledger list in one go instead of
+one-by-one form entry. This is the single biggest "automation" win on this
+list for a new-company setup flow.
+
+### Bulk Actions Toolbar
+Multi-select rows via checkboxes → toolbar appears with "Activate / Deactivate
+/ Delete selected".
+**Where:** any master table, once someone needs to deactivate 20 ledgers at
+once rather than one at a time.
+
+### Export (CSV / Excel / PDF)
+One button, exports the current filtered table view.
+**Where:** every master list and every report — accounting users expect to
+export a Trial Balance or Ledger list to Excel as a baseline feature, not an
+extra.
+
+### Print-friendly view
+A stripped-down, print-optimized layout (no sidebar/nav chrome).
+**Where:** vouchers, financial statements — these are commonly printed
+in real accounting workflows.
+
+---
+
+## 8. Code-Level Reusable Patterns (not visual, but equally high-leverage)
+
+### Generic CRUD API route factory
+A small helper that generates the standard `GET`/`POST`/`PATCH`/`DELETE`
+handlers (with the `P2002` unique-constraint handling and dependent-record
+delete guard you've already repeated across `account-groups`, `areas`,
+`sub-areas`) from a Prisma model name + a few config options.
+**Why now:** you're about to build Agent Master, then probably more masters
+after that — each one currently means writing near-identical route files by
+hand. This is the point where a shared factory starts paying for itself.
+
+### Config-driven Master Table/Form
+Instead of a bespoke `AreasTable`/`AreaForm` per model, a single
+`<MasterTable config={...}>` / `<MasterForm config={...}>` that takes a field
+list (label, type, validation) and renders consistently.
+**Trade-off to flag honestly:** this is powerful but also the one item here
+where over-abstracting too early can hurt — if every master needs slightly
+different business logic (like Sub-Group needing a cascading Account Group
+dropdown), a fully generic form can become harder to read than five explicit
+ones. Worth doing once you have 4–5 near-identical masters and can see the
+real shared shape, not before.
+
+### `useDebouncedSearch` hook
+Wraps a search input with a debounce timer before firing the API call.
+**Where:** any Async Combobox or server-driven Data Table.
+
+### `usePagination` hook
+Shared page/pageSize state + slice logic, instead of each table
+reimplementing `currentPage`/`pageSize`/`totalPages` math (currently
+duplicated verbatim across `AreasTable`, `SubAreasTable`, `GroupsTable`...).
+
+### Audit Trail viewer
+A generic component that renders `AuditLog` rows (old data vs. new data diff,
+who changed it, when) for any record.
+**Where:** the `AuditLog` model already exists in your schema with
+`oldData`/`newData`/`changedBy` — there's no UI for it yet anywhere. This is
+a good "modernness" win since it's already fully supported at the data layer.
+
+---
+
+## Suggested build order (highest leverage first)
+
+1. **Combobox** — every form you build from here on needs it.
+2. **Dynamic Line-Item Editor + Balance Indicator** — unlocks the entire
+   Transactions module (Journal/Cash-Bank Voucher, Sales, Purchase).
+3. **Generic CRUD API factory + `usePagination` hook** — stops the
+   copy-paste growing linearly with every new master.
+4. **Toast system** — small, but touches every form immediately.
+5. **Server-driven Data Table** — do this before Ledger/Party lists get big
+   enough that client-side filtering becomes visibly slow.
+6. **Command Palette** — biggest "feels modern" jump, but purely additive,
+   safe to do anytime once the nav tree is stable.
+7. Everything else (bulk import, tree view, audit viewer, fiscal year
+   switcher) — build when the feature that needs it comes up, not speculatively.
